.TH "PERFORMANCECONTAINERTIMING.IDENTIFIER" "3JS" "October 26, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
PerformanceContainerTiming.identifier \- PerformanceContainerTiming:
identifier property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]identifier\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]PerformanceContainerTiming\f[R] interface returns the value of the
\f[CR]containertiming\f[R] attribute on the container\(cqs root element.
.PP
This can be used to determine the container root that each entry belongs
to, which is useful if multiple containers are being reported at the
same time.
This approach is easier than comparing \f[CR]rootElement\f[R]
references.
.SH VALUE
A string.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Using \f[CR]identifier\f[R] to distinguish containers
This example shows how you can determine the affected container using
\f[CR]identifier\f[R].
.SS HTML
First we define two elements that are marked as container roots with the
\f[CR]containertiming\f[R] attribute, identified as
\f[CR]\(dqhero\(dq\f[R] and \f[CR]\(dqproduct\-list\(dq\f[R],
respectively.
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]section\f[R] containertiming=\(dqhero\(dq>
  <\f[B]h2\f[R]>Hero content</\f[B]h2\f[R]>
</\f[B]section\f[R]>
<\f[B]div\f[R] containertiming=\(dqproduct\-list\(dq>
  <\f[B]p\f[R]>Product list content</\f[B]p\f[R]>
</\f[B]div\f[R]>
.EE
.PP
Note that there is also hidden HTML (and code) for displaying log
information.
.SS JavaScript
The following code first checks whether the browser supports
\f[CR]\(dqcontainer\(dq\f[R] entries: if not, it logs that the feature
is not supported.
It then creates a \f[CR]PerformanceObserver\f[R] that logs the
\f[CR]identifier\f[R] and \f[CR]startTime\f[R] of each entry, allowing
the two containers to be told apart.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]if\f[R] (PerformanceObserver.supportedEntryTypes.includes(\(dqcontainer\(dq)) {
  \f[B]const\f[R] observer = \f[B]new\f[R] PerformanceObserver((list) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
    \f[B]for\f[R] (\f[B]const\f[R] entry \f[B]of\f[R] list.getEntries()) {
      log(\(ga${entry.identifier} painted at ${entry.startTime.toFixed(1)}\(ga);
    }
  });
  observer.observe({ type: \(dqcontainer\(dq, buffered: \f[B]true\f[R] });
} \f[B]else\f[R] {
  log(\(dqThis feature is not supported by your browser.\(dq);
}
.EE
.SS Result
The following log shows the \f[CR]identifier\f[R] and
\f[CR]startTime\f[R] reported for each of the two containers.
Note that the start time is the same in this case, as they are painted
in the same frame.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]containertiming\f[R] HTML attribute
